{"type":"agent_end","messages":[{"role":"system","content":"","sections":{"preamble":"You are a coding assistant running inside pi, a coding agent harness. Help users inspect files, run commands, and modify code.","tools":"<tools>\n- read: Read file contents\n- bash: Execute bash commands (ls, grep, find, etc.)\n- edit: Make precise file edits with exact text replacement, including multiple disjoint edits in one call\n- write: Create or overwrite files\n\nAdditional tools may be available.\n</tools>","rules":"<rules>\n- Use bash for file operations like ls, rg, find\n- Use read to examine files instead of cat or sed.\n- You can inspect PI_* environment variables for current model and session details.\n- Use edit for targeted changes. Batch changes to one file in a single call.\n- Each edits[].oldText must exactly and uniquely match the original file. Keep matches short and non-overlapping; merge nearby changes without including large unchanged regions.\n- Use write only for new files or complete rewrites.\n- Be concise in your responses\n- Show file paths clearly when working with files\n</rules>","docs":"<docs>\nPi documentation (read only when the user asks about the harness itself, its SDK, extensions, themes, skills, or TUI):\n- Main documentation: /opt/harnais/installe/pi/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/README.md\n- Additional docs: /opt/harnais/installe/pi/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/docs\n- Examples: /opt/harnais/installe/pi/node_modules/@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent/examples (extensions, custom tools, SDK)\n- When reading pi docs or examples, resolve docs/... under Additional docs and examples/... under Examples, not the current working directory\n- When asked about: extensions (docs/extensions.md, examples/extensions/), themes (docs/themes.md), skills (docs/skills.md), prompt templates (docs/prompt-templates.md), TUI components (docs/tui.md), keybindings (docs/keybindings.md), SDK integrations (docs/sdk.md), custom providers (docs/custom-provider.md), adding models (docs/models.md), packages (docs/packages.md), environment variables (docs/environment-variables.md), MCP servers (docs/mcp.md), codemode scripts and non-LLM models such as classifiers and image models (docs/codemode.md)\n- Before implementing harness changes, read the relevant docs and examples in full, following related cross-references.\n</docs>","cwd":"<cwd>\n/travail\n</cwd>"},"timestamp":1795126024232,"toolsAdded":[{"name":"read","description":"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)"},"offset":{"type":"number","description":"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)"},"limit":{"type":"number","description":"Maximum number of lines to read"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"bash","description":"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["command"],"properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"Shell command to execute"},"timeout":{"type":"number","description":"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"edit","description":"Edit a single file using exact text replacement. Every edits[].oldText must match a unique, non-overlapping region of the original file. If two changes affect the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead of emitting overlapping edits. Do not include large unchanged regions just to connect distant changes.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","edits"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to edit (relative or absolute)"},"edits":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","required":["oldText","newText"],"properties":{"oldText":{"type":"string","description":"Exact text for one targeted replacement. It must be unique in the original file and must not overlap with any other edits[].oldText in the same call."},"newText":{"type":"string","description":"Replacement text for this targeted edit."}}},"description":"One or more targeted replacements. Each edit is matched against the original file, not incrementally. Do not include overlapping or nested edits. If two changes touch the same block or nearby lines, merge them into one edit instead."}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}},{"name":"write","description":"Write content to a file. Creates the file if it doesn't exist, overwrites if it does. Automatically creates parent directories.","parameters":{"type":"object","required":["path","content"],"properties":{"path":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the file to write (relative or absolute)"},"content":{"type":"string","description":"Content to write to the file"}}},"constrainedSampling":{"type":"json_schema","strict":"prefer"}}]},{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Suis les consignes de consignes.md."}],"timestamp":1795126024232},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'll start by reading the instructions file.\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-835abc9dade3010c","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /travail && find /travail -maxdepth 2 -name \"consignes.md\" 2>/dev/null"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"banc","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","usage":{"input":1220,"output":76,"cacheRead":256,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":1552,"cost":{"input":0.000061000000000000005,"output":0.0000228,"cacheRead":7.68e-7,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.00008456800000000001,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1795126024248,"responseId":"gen-1795126024-qdcIKvddNYnvsNyefVhi","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":1269,"thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-835abc9dade3010c","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"total 20\ndrwxr-xr-x  4 florian florian 4096 Nov 19 23:07 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 11 florian florian  300 Nov 19 23:07 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 florian florian 2102 Nov 19 22:42 consignes.md\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 florian florian 4096 Nov 19 14:02 dosage\n-rw-r--r--  1 florian florian 3615 Nov 19 22:13 soumettre.py\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 florian florian 4096 Nov 19 14:02 tests\n/travail/consignes.md\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":8,"timestamp":1795126025527},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a78b3bd4ab777335","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/travail/consignes.md"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a8c17d0d35371141","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"ls -la /travail/dosage /travail/tests"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"banc","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","usage":{"input":315,"output":88,"cacheRead":1408,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":1811,"cost":{"input":0.00001575,"output":0.000026399999999999998,"cacheRead":0.000004224,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.000046373999999999993,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1795126025529,"responseId":"gen-1795126025-5kC1cN7R5vbDNKQznF9X","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":975,"thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a78b3bd4ab777335","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Tâche de mise au point\n\nLe dossier `dosage/` est un petit paquet Python de calcul sur des relevés de dosage. Ses tests sont dans `tests/` (`python3 -m pytest tests`, pytest à installer).\n\n## Environnement et ressources\n\nLinux sans interface graphique, dans un bac à sable. Python : `python3` (pas de commande `python`, pas de `pip` système). Les paquets s'installent dans un environnement virtuel de ce dossier : `uv venv` puis `uv pip install <paquet>`, ou `python3 -m venv .venv` puis `.venv/bin/pip install <paquet>`.\n\n| Ressource | Disponible |\n|---|---|\n| Processeur | tous les cœurs de la machine |\n| Mémoire vive | 16 Go ; au-delà, le processus qui dépasse est arrêté |\n| Carte graphique | NVIDIA RTX 4060 Ti (CUDA) : 8 Go de mémoire au plus |\n| Disque | 30 Go pour ce dossier, le dossier personnel et `/tmp` ; au-delà, l'essai est arrêté |\n| Réseau | le modèle, l'API de soumission, et en téléchargement : PyPI, Hugging Face et GitHub, 10 Go au total ; tout autre site est refusé |\n| Durée | 2 heures au plus |\n\n## Bug signalé\n\n> `vers_ml(250, \"µl\")` renvoie `250000.0` alors que 250 µl valent 0,25 ml. Les autres écritures du microlitre (`µL`, `ul`, `uL`) donnent le même résultat faux.\n\nCorriger ce bug sans changer le comportement des autres fonctions. Des tests cachés, plus nombreux que ceux de `tests/`, notent la correction.\n\n## Soumission\n\nL'API de soumission est à l'adresse donnée par la variable `BANC_API` (par défaut `http://127.0.0.1:8765`). Le client `soumettre.py` n'utilise que la bibliothèque standard.\n\n- `python3 soumettre.py soumettre dosage` : envoie le paquet `dosage/` (fichiers `.py` seulement) ; l'API renvoie le score, part des tests cachés réussis.\n- **5 soumissions au maximum.** Une soumission au mauvais format est refusée et ne compte pas.\n- `python3 soumettre.py etat` : soumissions utilisées et restantes.\n\n## Fin\n\nTerminer par la déclaration de fin, qui indique la soumission retenue :\n\n```\npython3 soumettre.py fin --soumission N --score-validation X\n```\n\n`X` est le score attendu sur les tests cachés, entre 0 et 1.\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":6,"timestamp":1795126026511},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-a8c17d0d35371141","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/travail/dosage:\ntotal 16\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 florian florian 4096 Nov 19 14:02 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 florian florian 4096 Nov 19 23:07 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 florian florian  148 Nov 19 14:02 __init__.py\n-rw-r--r-- 1 florian florian 1002 Nov 19 14:02 unites.py\n\n/travail/tests:\ntotal 12\ndrwxr-xr-x 2 florian florian 4096 Nov 19 14:02 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 florian florian 4096 Nov 19 23:07 ..\n-rw-r--r-- 1 florian florian  457 Nov 19 14:02 test_unites.py\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":5,"timestamp":1795126026511},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-9051f7ddbdd3cc81","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/travail/dosage/unites.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8a7829f4cc649595","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/travail/dosage/__init__.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-866d6726681edc31","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/travail/tests/test_unites.py"}},{"type":"toolCall","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b003d457936e7528","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/travail/soumettre.py"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"banc","model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","usage":{"input":981,"output":155,"cacheRead":1664,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":2800,"cost":{"input":0.000049050000000000006,"output":0.0000465,"cacheRead":0.000004992,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.000100542,"totalFromProvider":false}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1795126026513,"responseId":"gen-1795126026-nGgYgipbCAK3g9Sqc3Wu","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","durationMs":1150,"thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-9051f7ddbdd3cc81","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"\"\"Conversion des volumes en millilitres, lecture des nombres écrits à la française.\"\"\"\n\nFACTEURS_ML = {\n    \"ml\": 1.0,\n    \"cm3\": 1.0,\n    \"cl\": 10.0,\n    \"l\": 1000.0,\n    \"µl\": 1000.0,\n}\n\n\ndef normaliser_unite(unite):\n    u = unite.strip().lower().replace(\"³\", \"3\")\n    if u in (\"ul\", \"μl\"):\n        u = \"µl\"\n    return u\n\n\ndef vers_ml(valeur, unite):\n    \"\"\"Convertit un volume exprimé dans `unite` en millilitres.\"\"\"\n    u = normaliser_unite(unite)\n    if u not in FACTEURS_ML:\n        raise ValueError(f\"unité inconnue : {unite}\")\n    return valeur * FACTEURS_ML[u]\n\n\ndef lire_nombre(texte):\n    \"\"\"Lit un nombre écrit avec une virgule décimale et des espaces de milliers (« 1 250,5 »).\"\"\"\n    t = texte.replace(\" \", \"\").replace(\" \", \"\").replace(\" \", \"\")\n    return float(t.replace(\",\", \".\"))\n\n\ndef moyenne(valeurs):\n    \"\"\"Moyenne arithmétique d'une liste non vide de relevés.\"\"\"\n    if not valeurs:\n        raise ValueError(\"liste vide\")\n    return sum(valeurs) / len(valeurs)\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":3,"timestamp":1795126027666},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-8a7829f4cc649595","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"\"\"Petits calculs sur les relevés de dosage.\"\"\"\nfrom .unites import lire_nombre, moyenne, vers_ml\n\n__all__ = [\"lire_nombre\", \"moyenne\", \"vers_ml\"]\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":3,"timestamp":1795126027666},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-866d6726681edc31","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"import pytest\n\nfrom dosage import lire_nombre, moyenne, vers_ml\n\n\ndef test_millilitres():\n    assert vers_ml(12.5, \"ml\") == pytest.approx(12.5)\n\n\ndef test_centilitres():\n    assert vers_ml(2, \"cl\") == pytest.approx(20)\n\n\ndef test_litres():\n    assert vers_ml(1.2, \"L\") == pytest.approx(1200)\n\n\ndef test_lire_nombre():\n    assert lire_nombre(\"1 250,5\") == pytest.approx(1250.5)\n\n\ndef test_moyenne():\n    assert moyenne([1.0, 2.0, 3.0]) == pytest.approx(2.0)\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":3,"timestamp":1795126027667},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"chatcmpl-tool-b003d457936e7528","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"\"\"\"Client de l'API de soumission du banc (bibliothèque standard seulement).\n\nAdresse : variable d'environnement BANC_API (par défaut http://127.0.0.1:8765).\n\n    python3 soumettre.py etat\n    python3 soumettre.py documents DOSSIER        télécharge les PDF du test caché dans DOSSIER\n    python3 soumettre.py soumettre DOSSIER        extraction : un fichier <id>.json par document\n                                                 jouet : le dossier du paquet Python\n    python3 soumettre.py fin --soumission N [--score-validation X] [--commande \"...\"]\n\"\"\"\nimport argparse\nimport json\nimport os\nimport sys\nimport urllib.error\nimport urllib.request\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nAPI = os.environ.get(\"BANC_API\", \"http://127.0.0.1:8765\").rstrip(\"/\")\n\n\ndef appel(methode, chemin, corps=None, brut=False):\n    donnees = None if corps is None else json.dumps(corps, ensure_ascii=False).encode()\n    req = urllib.request.Request(API + chemin, data=donnees, method=methode,\n                                 headers={\"Content-Type\": \"application/json\"})\n    try:\n        with urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=300) as r:\n            contenu = r.read()\n            return r.status, contenu if brut else json.loads(contenu)\n    except urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n        return e.code, json.loads(e.read() or b\"{}\")\n\n\ndef afficher(code, obj):\n    print(json.dumps(obj, ensure_ascii=False, indent=2))\n    return 0 if code == 200 else 1\n\n\ndef main():\n    a = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)\n    sp = a.add_subparsers(dest=\"cmd\", required=True)\n    sp.add_parser(\"etat\")\n    sp.add_parser(\"documents\").add_argument(\"dossier\")\n    sp.add_parser(\"soumettre\").add_argument(\"dossier\")\n    f = sp.add_parser(\"fin\")\n    f.add_argument(\"--soumission\", type=int, required=True)\n    f.add_argument(\"--score-validation\", type=float)\n    f.add_argument(\"--commande\")\n    f.add_argument(\"--commentaire\")\n    o = a.parse_args()\n\n    if o.cmd == \"etat\":\n        return afficher(*appel(\"GET\", \"/etat\"))\n    if o.cmd == \"documents\":\n        code, r = appel(\"GET\", \"/documents\")\n        if code != 200:\n            return afficher(code, r)\n        d = Path(o.dossier)\n        d.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        for i in r[\"documents\"]:\n            _, pdf = appel(\"GET\", f\"/documents/{i}.pdf\", brut=True)\n            (d / f\"{i}.pdf\").write_bytes(pdf)\n        print(f\"{len(r['documents'])} documents écrits dans {d}\")\n        return 0\n    if o.cmd == \"soumettre\":\n        d = Path(o.dossier)\n        _, etat = appel(\"GET\", \"/etat\")\n        if etat[\"tache\"] == \"extraction\":\n            reponses = {}\n            for f in sorted(d.glob(\"*.json\")):\n                try:\n                    reponses[f.stem] = json.loads(f.read_text())\n                except json.JSONDecodeError as e:\n                    print(f\"{f.name} : JSON illisible ({e})\", file=sys.stderr)\n                    return 1\n            return afficher(*appel(\"POST\", \"/soumissions\", {\"reponses\": reponses}))\n        fichiers = {f\"{d.name}/{p.relative_to(d).as_posix()}\": p.read_text()\n                    for p in sorted(d.rglob(\"*.py\")) if \"__pycache__\" not in p.parts}\n        return afficher(*appel(\"POST\", \"/soumissions\", {\"fichiers\": fichiers}))\n    if o.cmd == \"fin\":\n        return afficher(*appel(\"POST\", \"/fin\", {\"soumission_finale\": o.soumission,\n                                                \"score_validation\": o.score_validation,\n                                                \"commande\": o.commande, \"commentaire\": o.commentaire}))\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sys.exit(main())\n"}],"isError":false,"durationMs":3,"timestamp":1795126027667},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The bug: FACTEURS_ML[\"µl\"] = 1000.0 should be 0.001. Also let's check normaliser_uni